            "desc": "Set the `registryApp` ID. Admin only. Validates the new registry exposes an `admin` key\nbefore binding, so a bad `appId` can't brick role resolution. Note an nonexistent app will\nrevert on `app_global_get_ex`, so new registry must exist and have an `admin` key.\nThis is a migration path for the registry app. Always set the new registry before deleting\nthe old one (if so), never after - as admin auth could be bricked.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "withdrawALGO",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "address",
                    "name": "receiver",
                    "desc": "Destination account"
                },
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "amount",
                    "desc": "microALGO to withdraw"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Withdraw ALGO from the instance app account to `receiver`. Admin only.\nThe AVM rejects the inner payment if it would drop the app account below its min\nbalance, so over-withdrawal fails atomically (no explicit balance check needed).",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
